  "finalText": "The canonical sequence of P04637 is 393 amino acids long, and the EBI Proteins API isoforms endpoint returns 9 isoform entries for it. Both numbers come from live rightclick-x calls.\n\n- **Canonical length:** A UniProtKB REST search for `accession:P04637` returned a sequence length of 393.\n- **Isoform entries:** The Proteins API isoforms endpoint returned an array of 9 entries, P04637-1 through P04637-9. Their lengths are 393, 341, 346, 354, 302, 307, 261, 209 and 214 respectively.\n\nThe 9 includes P04637-1, which is the canonical isoform itself, so there are 8 alternative isoforms on top of it.\n\nANSWER: 393 | 9"
